      "description": "Watch Stevenage vs Luton Town highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 11, 2026. The League One clash between Stevenage and Luton Town on September 11, 2026, delivered a masterclass in grit and tactical execution. Both sides entered the fray with high stakes, creating an atmosphere charged with anticipation from the opening whistle. Kemp Ignites the First Half The match began with a fiery tempo, as the referee was forced to reach for his pocket as early as the 4th minute to caution Daniel Phillips . Despite the stop-start nature of the early exchanges, Stevenage found their rhythm in the 23rd minute when Dan Kemp clinical finish put the home side ahead. The opening period remained physical, with Lewis Freestone and Dan Kemp receiving yellow cards for the hosts, while Liam Walsh was booked for Luton Town as they struggled to contain the pressure before the break. Second Half Drama and Goal Exchanges As the second half got underway, both managers turned to their benches to find a spark. The momentum swung further in favor of Stevenage in the 70th minute when Josh Magennis doubled the lead with a well-taken goal. However, any thoughts of a comfortable finish were quickly dispelled. Just five minutes later, Kasey Palmer turned provider, setting up Mads Juel Andersen to pull one back for Luton Town , setting the stage for a frantic final fifteen minutes. Gritty Finish Under Pressure The closing stages were a test of nerves, characterized by desperate defending and tactical fouls. Saxon Earley and Luther Wildin were both cautioned as Stevenage looked to disrupt the visitors' flow. Even Mads Juel Andersen , the goalscorer for the visitors, found himself in the book during stoppage time. Despite seven minutes of added time and relentless pressure from the Hatters, the home side held firm to secure all three points in a memorable encounter."
